Abbreviation:
  a Direction is
    an index in [0, 4).

Abbreviation:
  n is
    (0 : Direction).

Abbreviation:
  s is
    (1 : Direction).

Abbreviation:
  e is
    (2 : Direction).

Abbreviation:
  w is
    (3 : Direction).

Abbreviation:
  a Tile is
    a function from Direction to ℕ.

Definition:
  a list T of Tile elements satisfies TilesPlane if
    there is a function t from ℤ and ℤ to Tile such that
      for all integers x and y:
        t x y ∈ T and t x y e = t (x + 1) y w and t x y n = t x (y + 1) s.

Definition:
  CoRE is
    the function mapping an implicit element α of Type u_1 and an instance of typeclass Primcodable α and a function p from α to Prop to
      (the function mapping an element x of α to
        x does not satisfy p) is recursively enumerable.

Definition:
  CoREComplete is
    the function mapping an implicit element α of Type u_1 and an instance of typeclass Primcodable α and a function p from α to Prop to
      p satisfies CoRE and
      for every function q from ℕ to Prop satisfying CoRE:
        there is a function r from ℕ to α such that
          r is computable and
          for every natural number n:
            n satisfies q if and only if (r n) satisfies p.

Theorem coRE_complete:
  TilesPlane satisfies CoREComplete

Theorem undecidable:
  TilesPlane is not computable
